$DIR/main.p:14:9: invalid operation: operator + does not apply to *f (variable of int32 type Fd), an owner; convert it to read its value: int32(*f)
    An operator other than a comparison is applied to a value of an owner type.
    An owner may be compared, but no other operator applies to it, whatever its
    underlying type: f + 1 for type Fd owner int32 would be a new Fd made by
    arithmetic, a second owner of whatever the first refers to.
    Convert the owner to its underlying type, which reads its value and moves
    nothing, and apply the operator to the result.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    (see "Operators" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.18)
    (run "pluto explain E3214" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:19:8: invalid operation: operator - does not apply to f (variable of int32 type Fd), an owner; convert it to read its value: int32(f)
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E3214" for more)

